<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Discovering an Area Model</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01555</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Discovering an Area Model</md:title>
    <md:uuid>589dbb11-c809-4136-bef3-b42ab4fe46eb</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <note id="note-00001">
        <para id="para-00001"><link url="https://phet.colorado.edu/sims/html/area-model-algebra/latest/area-model-algebra_en.html?screens=1,2,3">Access the interactive simulator </link>to begin this project.</para></note>
      
      <para id="para-00002">In this activity, whenever you see 💬, stop and share your responses with your partner. If you have different responses, try to come to a consensus.</para>
      <para id="para-00003">Today you are going to investigate something called an interactive simulation. It is a tool that will help you visualize how area model multiplication works.</para>
      <para id="para-00004">
          <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
            <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_07_03_02_01.png"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <para id="para-00005"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - <link url="https://phet.colorado.edu/sims/html/area-model-algebra/latest/area-model-algebra_en.html?screens=1,2,3">Open the interactive simulator</link>, Area Model Algebra in your web browser. You will use it to complete this project. It will look like the image above.</para>
      <para id="para-00006"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Play with any of the screens on Area Model Algebra for 5 minutes.</para>
      <para id="para-00007"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Complete the following questions.</para>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00001">
        <item>What does the area of a rectangle have to do with multiplication? 💬</item>

        <item>Write down two things you notice or have questions about, and one thing a neighbor noticed that is interesting to you.</item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </content>
